{"The event listener is guarded by the ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ feature flag, while all other logic in this class (including management(...)) is controlled by ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2; this mismatch means that when only the V2 feature is enabled the listener will never run, so permissions won't be cleaned up on role/client/group removal": 0.7171391844749451, "The method that collects client identifiers with a given permission iterates over all resources of type 'clients', including the type-level 'all-clients' resource, so when global permissions are granted it will incorrectly add the type-level resource name (e.g. 'clients') to the returned set instead of only real client resources, leading callers that expect actual client IDs to misbehave or see inconsistent access control": 0.8573471903800964}